-daemon-process.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_sharded_daemon_process_wake_up_messages", "label": "Wake-up messages", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Internal wake-ups to every index force the sharding machinery to materialize each daemon eagerly on the node the coordinator chose, instead of waiting for real traffic.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/sharded-daemon-process.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_sharded_daemon_process_cardinality_rule", "label": "Right tool by cardinality", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "1 goes to a singleton (explicit election/lease guarantees), fixed N to the daemon process, one-per-business-entity to sharding, and every-node to a cluster router.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/sharded-daemon-process.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_sharded_daemon_process_deterministic_by_index", "label": "Each daemon's behavior must be deterministic by index", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The factory must produce the same behavior for the same index, otherwise a failover gives a different daemon 3 than before.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/sharded-daemon-process.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_sharded_daemon_process_reconciler", "label": "Reconciler (per-index daemon example)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/sharded-daemon-process.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "